  "question": {
    "text": "A TV transmission tower antenna is at a height&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. Suppose that the receiving antenna is&nbsp;at.<br />(i) ground level<br />(ii) a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.<br />The increase in antenna range in case (ii)&nbsp;relative to case (i) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>%</mo></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>, to the nearest integer, is."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "50",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Range (i)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Range (ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msqrt></math></p><p>where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Ans <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msqrt><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mn>20</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"
  }
